    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="0993" n="977" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg977"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/5–449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Israel</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McDonald</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential   us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tel Aviv</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-04T14:00:00+03:00">May 4, 1949—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>332. At state dinner May 3 Sharett asked me report to Department in strictest
                    confidence that special meeting Israel-Syrian armistice negotiators to be held
                    May 5 without presence UN officials at request Syria. Foreign Minister regards
                    this as crucial test. He pleads for US good offices [garble] urge Colonel Zaim
                    not insist on “rectification” of frontier. If this demand is withdrawn, Foreign
                    Minister optimistic agreement armistice and prospect of peace negotiations.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Comment:</hi> I hope Department can act promptly.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d634-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">End Comment</hi>.</p>
                <pb facs="0994" n="978" xml:id="pg978"/>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">New subject:</hi> Foreign Minister told me that Israel
                    expects issue either New York or Lausanne new and comprehensive refugee
                    statement. <hi rendition="#italic">Comment:</hi> I hope but I cannot be sure it
                    will be conciliatory. <hi rendition="#italic">End comment</hi>.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d634-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McDonald</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d634-f1" n="1" xml:id="d634-f1-content">
                <p>The editors have found no evidence in the Department of State files that it
                    ordered the exercise of the good offices of the United States in this matter. On
                    May 7, the Department advised Tel Aviv of its anxiety to receive information
                    concerning the outcome of the Israeli-Syrian meeting of May 5 (telegram 280,
                    867N.01/5–449). In reply, on May 10, Ambassador McDonald stated he had been
                    advised by General Riley that the “meeting was complete failure. Neither side
                    would budge.” (telegram 347, 867N.01/5–1049)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d634-f2" n="2" xml:id="d634-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably the statement by Mr. Eytan as reported in <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
